WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.600
The rest of this gate ties the
card's life to the person's.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.350
No card is requested without
a joiner record and a sponsor.

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.747
The card system writes the
binding when the card is issued,

4
00:00:10.747 --> 00:00:13.012
and removes it when the card is revoked.

5
00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:17.847
Once the binding lands, the temporary pass
from gate three isn't needed anymore,

6
00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:20.674
and the proofing level
is recorded per person.

7
00:00:20.674 --> 00:00:24.625
The card system's events flow
back in, keyed on the person key.

8
00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:28.797
Those events are termination,
revocation, suspension and expiry,

9
00:00:28.797 --> 00:00:31.888
and the same event can
mean two different things.

10
00:00:31.888 --> 00:00:36.562
For a contractor, a terminated or
expired card ends the engagement.

11
00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:40.275
For an employee, it's credential
drift, not a separation,

12
00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:43.575
because only HR decides
when an employee leaves.

13
00:00:43.575 --> 00:00:46.225
And a legal name change
rewrites the binding.

14
00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:49.324
The guide is open that the
card system's interface,

15
00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:52.630
and the contractor PIV path,
are still pending proof.
